.TH "REPROCTL" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl \- unified CLI for local development with Tilt, kind, and git
worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]] \f[I]command\f[R]
[\f[I]args\f[R]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
reproctl manages the local development environment for the Repro
monorepo.
It handles cluster lifecycle, service orchestration via Tilt, database
operations, git worktree management, and log streaming.
.PP
Context is detected automatically: from the main checkout, services run
as main; from a worktree, services are isolated to that branch.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Output machine\-readable JSON instead of human\-readable text.
Supported by: \f[B]checkhealth\f[R], \f[B]cluster status\f[R],
\f[B]context\f[R], \f[B]db status\f[R], \f[B]doctor\f[R],
\f[B]logs\f[R], \f[B]status\f[R], \f[B]wt list\f[R].
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Environment
.TP
\f[B]setup\f[R]
Bootstrap the development environment.
See \f[B]reproctl\-setup\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]doctor\f[R]
Diagnose the development environment.
See \f[B]reproctl\-doctor\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]checkhealth\f[R] [\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]]
Runtime health checks (Tilt, k8s, services).
.SS Services
.TP
\f[B]start\f[R] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]...]
Start services from the current context.
See \f[B]reproctl\-start\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]stop\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]...] | \f[B]\-\-all\f[R]
Stop services or tear down Tilt.
See \f[B]reproctl\-stop\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]restart\f[R] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]...] | \f[B]\-\-all\f[R]
Rebuild services or restart the Tilt daemon.
See \f[B]reproctl\-restart\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Show running services and Tilt dashboard URL.
With \f[B]\-\-json\f[R], outputs a JSON object with Tilt state and a
